INSERT INTO feature VALUES('derivation-view','editor','The derivation pane at the cursor','derivation-index','implemented','uncommon','mainstream editors','`gandr view --trace` asks the hub for the trace layer at the width of its terminal. While the view is attached, the hub judges each job at that layer and sends the derivation card of the declaration at the editor''s cursor, once for each declaration that the cursor enters. The first view makes each connection judge its documents again at that layer, so a view that attaches after the editor''s last job hears the card with no edit. The pane draws one line for each judgement node in the blueprint''s columns: the warrant, the direction, the goal set in by its depth, the type, the rule, the cover, the memo mark, the nodes visited and the wall time. The hub prints each goal and type on one line, with no layout, and cuts it to the room of its column, so a card costs a print of its goals and nothing more. The path from a root to the node at the cursor is open and each other subtree folds. Enter opens the node in focus: the view asks the hub for its whole goal, and the hub lays out that one goal at the width of the view. A hover at the trace layer ends with the same path, each goal on one line.','surface-session surface-render-remote surface-lsp surface-lsp-core surface-tui surface-driver','crates/surface-render-remote/src/derivation.rs crates/surface-lsp-core/src/derivation.rs crates/surface-lsp/src/hub.rs crates/surface-lsp/src/server.rs crates/surface-tui/src/follow.rs crates/surface-tui/tests/captures.rs','crate-tests','#6295');
